spans.s:
शय शय, अस्, आ or ई, अम् (fr. rt. 1. शी), ly-
ing down, asleep, sleeping; (अस्), m. sleep, sleeping;
a bed, couch; a hand; a snake, the boa constrictor;
abuse, imprecation; (according to Śabda-k.) = पण;
(आ), f., Ved. a place of rest or repose, [cf. सय्या;
cf. also Gr. ὀρέσ-κοιος.]

शयु, उस्, उस्, उ, lying down, reclining, sleeping;
(उस्), m. a large snake, the boa constrictor; N. of
a person protected by the Aśvins.

सयत्न स-यत्न, अस्, आ, अम्, making efforts,
taking pains, endeavouring, persevering; active, busy;
(अम्), ind. with effort, vigorously, assiduously.

सायम्प्रातिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. सायम्-प्रातर्;
cf. पौनःपुनिक), belonging to evening and
morning.
